.TH GETLYRICSMCP 1 "July 2026" "getlyricsmcp 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
getlyricsmcp \- MCP server that finds and fetches song lyrics
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B getlyricsmcp
.RB [ \-V | \-\-version ]
.RB [ \-h | \-\-help ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B getlyricsmcp
is a Model Context Protocol server speaking the stdio transport. It takes no
arguments and is meant to be spawned by an MCP client, not run interactively.
Run by hand it will simply wait for JSON-RPC on standard input.
.PP
It exposes two tools. There is no search API behind either of them and no API key
is required anywhere: the song-page URL for each source is constructed from the
given artist and title, requested, and kept if it resolves.
.SH TOOLS
.TP
.BI search_lyrics( artist , title )
Probes every source in parallel and returns the candidates that resolved, sorted
most-reliable-first. Each hit carries an
.I id
to pass to
.BR get_lyrics .
Sources known to answer 200 with an unrelated page instead of 404ing have their
page title verified, and mismatches are dropped before the hit list is returned.
.TP
.BI get_lyrics( id )
Fetches and parses the full lyrics text for one hit. The text is fetched fresh
from the source on every call and is never written to disk or cached.
.SH SOURCES
azlyrics.com and genius.com (English), versuri.ro and versuri.us (Romanian),
lyricshare.net (Russian), tekstowo.pl (Polish), letras.mus.br (Portuguese),
sarkisozum.gen.tr (Turkish), klyrics.net (Korean), paroles.net (French),
angolotesti.it (Italian), letras.com (Spanish), and soundcloud.com track
descriptions.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print version and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print usage and exit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B RUST_LOG
Tracing filter, for example
.BR RUST_LOG=debug .
Log output goes to standard error so it cannot corrupt the JSON-RPC stream on
standard output.
.SH EXAMPLES
Register with Claude Code for the current project:
.PP
.RS
.EX
claude mcp add getlyricsmcp \-\- getlyricsmcp
.EE
.RE
.PP
Register globally:
.PP
.RS
.EX
claude mcp add \-s user getlyricsmcp \-\- getlyricsmcp
.EE
.RE
.SH NOTES
Lyrics are copyrighted, and the sites this reads have their own terms of service
and robots.txt. Checking the terms of any source you point it at is the operator's
responsibility. Sources are one row of data each in
.IR src/sites/spec.rs ;
deleting a row removes the source.
